    "field": "Numerical methods for geophysical fluid dynamics",
    "problem": "The spectral element method, while an efficient high-order method, produces undesirable oscillations from its advection operator, making it unsuitable for many applications that require non-oscillatory solutions.",
    "method": "We propose a non-oscillatory advection scheme for the compatible spectral element method by introducing a local, conservative, element-wise reconstruction step within a continuous Galerkin formulation to eliminate the method's inherent oscillations.",
    "task": "The task is to develop a non-oscillatory advection operator for the compatible spectral element method by implementing a local, conservative reconstruction procedure to eliminate spurious oscillations produced by the standard method.",
